{"diagnosis": "Trace shows 256 NOP fetches ending in `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `tohost: FAIL 0xdead` instead of sequential fetch progress. `mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle` at picorv32.v:384 selects stale `mem_rdata_q` while `mem_xfer` is asserted instead of fresh `mem_rdata`, and volatile `mem_rdata` after xfer instead of held `q`, mis-decoding to illegal. CONE_SLICE picosoc/picosoc.v:127-132 only shows SoC `mem_ready`/`mem_rdata` mux and does not explain the stale fetch, so trace wins and root cause is inverted `mem_xfer` polarity in the latch mux.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384,1 +384,1 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (!mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no `TRAP: cpu trap asserted`, checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659"}

